    <!-- GeneralsX @feature Android port accent-colors 16/10/2026 The DARKMODE
         halves of the alternate accent palettes offered by the launcher's
         Interface -> Accent picker (ThemeHelper). The default violet lives in
         the base values-night/colors.xml and needs no overlay. Names mirror
         values/accent_colors.xml exactly: keep the two lists in sync.

         GeneralsX @feature Android port navy-theme 19/10/2026 The WALLS are
         now the navy theme's own surface ladder, identical for every accent
         (values-night/colors.xml): deep-sea ground #06111D, surface #0A1726,
         the four container steps up to #1C3249, brine-blue hairlines. Before
         this, each accent carried a near-black hue wash of its own, so
         choosing an accent replaced the whole background; on the navy theme
         that would have quietly undone the port on eleven of the twelve
         accent choices, including the default-adjacent dark ones.

         What still changes per accent is what should: the primary and its
         container (buttons, selected drawer rows, tabs, switches, sliders,
         focus states), the matching ripple, and the secondary pair. The
         surfaces are shared so the app is recognisably the same navy theme
         whichever accent is picked, and the text roles in
         values-night/colors.xml (cool whites, blue-greys) are the ones these
         accents were contrast-checked against.

         Daylight halves in values/accent_colors.xml are untouched: they keep
         their pale hue washes on the light palette, which is what the
         Daylight mode is. -->

